<</Producer(iText® 5.5.5 ©2000-2014 iText Group NV \(AGPL-version\))/Title(SOME U.S. FOREIGN-SERVICE OFFICERS ARE STILL HOPPING MAD OVER THE STATE DEPARTMENT'S COVER-UP OF THE SOVIETS' BEAMING OF MICROWAVES INTO THE MOSCOW EMBASSY.)/Keywords( M In III    _  L  1\r\n Declassified and Approved For Release 2012/05/10: CIA-RDP88B01125R000300120055-1\r\n U.S. IIL`::S ,.WORLD REPO-;;,T\r\n 21 June 176\r\n Washington Whisperse\r\n Some .U.S. foreign-service officers are\r\n still hopping mad over the State De-\r\n partment's cover-up of the Soviets'\r\n beaming of microwaves into the Mos-\r\n cow Embassy. Says one. "No one ever\r\n warned us of the microwave risks\r\n when we were serving in the Embas-\r\n sy, or even warned us after we left.-\r\n Declassified and Approved For Release 2012/05/10: CIA-RDP88B01125R000300120055-1\r\n)/Subject(SOME U.S. FOREIGN-SERVICE OFFICERS ARE STILL HOPPING MAD OVER THE STATE DEPARTMENT'S COVER-UP OF THE SOVIETS' BEAMING OF MICROWAVES INTO THE MOSCOW EMBASSY.)/ModDate(D:20161223022200Z)/CreationDate(D:20161223022200Z)>>
